'' =====================================================================
''
''   File....... e3-group0-idle-band-test.spin2
''   Purpose.... Decide on SILICON whether cogs 0-3 show the same E3 band
''               when EVERY cog of 0-3 is stopped across wraps while
''               cogs 4-7 run, and whether it closes in one wrap there
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 27 Sep 2026
''
'' =====================================================================

{ WHAT IS KNOWN (erratum E3, ledger EF-068):
    The erratum was measured in the cogs 4-7 group only.  Cog 0 runs
    from reset, so the cogs 0-3 group was never tested with every one of
    its cogs stopped; the chapter says so.

  THE QUESTION THIS TEST DECIDES:
    The design study's reading is symmetric: each group of four holds
    its own copy, refreshed at a wrap only while a cog of THAT group
    runs.  So if every cog of 0-3 stops and cogs 4-7 keep running, cogs
    0-3 should show the same band: a cog of 0-3 started after the group
    missed k wraps reads the upper long k behind, until the first wrap
    the group runs through, which closes it in one step.

  HOW COGS 0-3 ARE EMPTIED: cog 0 checks the boot state, starts the
    controller -- this program's Spin2 test code -- in cog 4 with
    COGSPIN, and then stops itself.  From then on the controller in cog
    4 is the reference: it started before the first wrap and never
    stops, so its group is current (C2 checks it on every poll).

  RIG: bare P2 board (20 MHz crystal assumed by _clkfreq), NO pin, NO
    jumper, nothing attached.  No pin is driven; P56..P63 untouched
    (P62/P63 are the DEBUG serial link, owned by the debugger).

  COGS (every start names its cog -- never the free-cog form):
    cog 0      boot check, starts the controller, then COGSTOPs itself
    cog 4      CTRL_COG, the controller and the reference; debugger here
    cog 5      REF_SMP_COG, group-1 control sampler, from start to end
    cog 1      SMP_COG_A, group-0 sampler, started in the band, never stopped
    cog 3      SMP_COG_B, group-0 sampler, started in the band, never stopped
    DEBUG_COGS = cogs 0 and 4: cog 0 prints the boot line, cog 4 the rest.
    No sampler takes a debug interrupt (EF-057).  The reference cog
    carries the debugger here as cog 0 does in every sibling test: it
    calls debug() only between pairs, and a pair whose two reference
    reads straddle a stall is discarded by the window check.
    If cog 0 is stopped while holding the DEBUG output lock (LOCK[15]),
    the lock goes free when the cog stops, so cog 4 cannot hang on it.

  DEFINITIONS (the measuring engine of the E3 Run A / Run B programs,
  with the reference moved from cog 0 to cog 4):
    pair  = cog 4 reads its own CT (GETCT WC then GETCT: refB), writes a
            request number to the sampler's hub mailbox, the sampler
            answers with its own GETCT WC then GETCT, then ack = request;
            cog 4 reads the sampler's longs after seeing the ack, then
            reads its own CT again (refA).
    valid = refB.hi == refA.hi and refB.lo, sampler.lo, refA.lo all in
            [$1000_0000, $F000_0000] (well clear of any wrap).
    D     = refB.hi - sampler.hi
    LO-BRACKET = refB.lo < sampler.lo < refA.lo (unsigned).
    A reading = 10 valid pairs, all printed raw.

  ARMS, in run order (hi = cog 4's own CT upper long; L = LAG = 2):
    boot   (cog 0) CT hi must be 0; running = cog 0 only
    start  (cog 0) controller in cog 4; cog 0 stops itself
    start  (cog 4) cog 5 = group-1 control sampler; running = cogs 4, 5
    R0     hi=0 early: cog 5 control
    (cogs 0-3: NO cog running through wraps 0->1 ... (L-1)->L)
    --- cogs 1 and 3 started at hi=L: the band opens in group 0 ---
    B1E/B3E  hi=L   early: cog 1, cog 3   band: TRUE L / FALSE 0
    B1L/B3L  hi=L   late:  cog 1, cog 3   band: TRUE L
    (cogs 1 and 3 run through wrap L->L+1: the closing wrap)
    X1E/X3E  hi=L+1 early: cog 1, cog 3   closed: TRUE 0 / FALSE L-1 or L
    X1L/X3L  hi=L+1 late:  cog 1, cog 3   closed: TRUE 0
    (cogs 1 and 3 run through wrap L+1->L+2)
    Y1E/Y3E  hi=L+2 early: cog 1, cog 3   stays closed: TRUE 0
    Every group-0 reading is paired with a cog-5 control reading.

  IN-RUN CONTROLS THAT GATE THE VERDICT (any failure -> "RIG FAIL", no
  verdict):
    C1  cog 5 (group 1) D == 0, status ok, in every control reading.
    C2  cog 4's upper long == the lower-long wraps cog 4 itself watched
        since it started at hi = 0 (every poll in the window).
    C3  running-cog mask polled on every wait and checked after every
        start: exactly the cogs this program started.  No cog of 0-3 may
        run before hi = L -- cog 0 included.
    C4  boot (cog 0): CT hi == 0 (fresh reset), running = cog 0 only;
        controller start (cog 4): CT hi == 0.
    C5  every request answered within 100 ms (sampler alive).

  VERDICT (one line, fixed before the run):
    CONFIRMED     all four band readings D = L, all six readings after
                  the closing wrap D = 0, all status ok: cogs 0-3 show the
                  same band as cogs 4-7, and it closes in one wrap
    REFUTED       a group-0 reading consistent (10 agreeing pairs) with
                  any other D (printed, with the arm that broke), or a
                  group-0 LO-BRACKET failure
    INCONCLUSIVE  a group-0 reading whose pairs disagree or that got too
                  few valid pairs
    RIG FAIL      any of C1..C5 failed: NO VERDICT

  CLOCK / RUN TIME: _clkfreq = 200_000_000 -> 2^32 clocks = 21.47 s per
    wrap.  The run ends at CT hi = L+2 = 4, lo just past $1000_0000:
    about 4.06 x 21.47 s = ~87 s after reset (plus download).

  HOW TO RUN: download to RAM with DEBUG enabled (pnut-term-ts, or PNut
    with debug on: Ctrl-F10).  The download must RESET the P2 (the
    counter must start from zero).  Do not reload while running.  After
    the boot line, every line comes from cog 4.  Read the final VERDICT
    line; all raw pairs are printed above it.  The run ends with
    DEBUG_END_SESSION.

  COMPILER: pnut-ts v1.55.8,  pnut-ts -d e3-group0-idle-band-test.spin2
}

CON ' ---- Test Configuration ----
  _clkfreq    = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS  = %0001_0001        ' debugger in cog 0 (boot line) and cog 4 (controller) only

  LAG     = 2                     ' wraps the cogs 0-3 group misses before its first sampler starts

  LOWIN   = $1000_0000            ' sample window: lowest CT lower long a pair may use
  HIWIN   = $F000_0000            ' sample window: highest CT lower long a pair may use
  LATE    = $E000_0000            ' late-in-epoch reading point (inside window)
  NPAIRS  = 10                    ' valid pairs per reading
  MAXTRY  = 30                    ' request attempts per reading

  ACK_TIMEOUTS_PER_SEC = 10       ' C5: a sampler must ack within clkfreq / 10 clocks (100 ms)
  COG_SETTLE_MS  = 10             ' wait after a COGINIT before checking the mask
  COG_COUNT      = 8              ' cogs 0..7 on a P2
  LONG_BITS      = 32             ' bits in a long
  NIB_BITS       = 4              ' "alive" throttle: hi and the top nibble of lo
  ALIVE_SHIFT    = LONG_BITS - NIB_BITS   ' brings lo's top nibble down to bits 3..0
  BOOL_BIT       = 1              ' low bit of TRUE (-1): prints a flag as 1 or 0
  CTRL_STACK_LONGS = 512          ' the controller's Spin2 stack

  ' mailbox layout, in longs: [0]=request [1]=hi [2]=lo [3]=ack
  MB_LONGS   = 4                  ' longs per mailbox
  MB_HI_IDX  = 1                  ' long index of the hi long (the sampler's PTRA[MB_HI_IDX])
  MB_LO_IDX  = 2                  ' long index of the lo long
  MB_ACK_IDX = 3                  ' long index of the ack long
  MB_HI_OFS  = MB_HI_IDX * 4      ' byte offsets of the hi, lo and ack longs
  MB_LO_OFS  = MB_LO_IDX * 4
  MB_ACK_OFS = MB_ACK_IDX * 4

  ' the rig's cogs, each started by its explicit number
  BOOT_COG    = 0                 ' boot check; stops itself
  CTRL_COG    = 4                 ' the controller and the reference
  REF_SMP_COG = 5                 ' group-1 control sampler
  SMP_COG_A   = 1                 ' group-0 samplers under test
  SMP_COG_B   = 3

  ' expected running-cog masks
  M_BOOT  = 1 << BOOT_COG                                 ' cog 0 alone
  M_REF   = (1 << CTRL_COG) | (1 << REF_SMP_COG)          ' cogs 4 and 5: cogs 0-3 empty
  M_BAND  = M_REF | (1 << SMP_COG_A) | (1 << SMP_COG_B)   ' + both group-0 samplers

  ' reading status codes (readStatus[] value per slot)
  '  ST_OK      - status ok, D consistent across all valid pairs
  '  ST_BRACKET - LO-BRACKET failed on >= 1 valid pair (lower copy not current)
  '  ST_MIXED   - valid pairs disagreed on D
  '  ST_SHORT   - fewer than NPAIRS valid pairs before MAXTRY
  '  ST_TIMEOUT - sampler never acked a request
  ST_OK = 0, ST_BRACKET = 1, ST_MIXED = 2, ST_SHORT = 3, ST_TIMEOUT = 4

  ' take_pair() ack status (a status code, not a boolean):
  '  ACK_NONE - the sampler did not ack within the timeout
  '  ACK_SEEN - the sampler acked
  #0, ACK_NONE, ACK_SEEN

  ' reading slots (index into readStatus[], readD[] and readBracketFails[]):
  '  R_C0  - R0: cog 5 at hi=0, control (C1)
  '  R_B1E, R_B3E, R_CBE - band, hi=LAG early: cog 1, cog 3, cog 5 control
  '  R_B1L, R_B3L, R_CBL - band, hi=LAG late
  '  R_X1E, R_X3E, R_CXE - after the closing wrap, hi=LAG+1 early
  '  R_X1L, R_X3L, R_CXL - after the closing wrap, hi=LAG+1 late
  '  R_Y1E, R_Y3E, R_CYE - one wrap later, hi=LAG+2 early
  R_C0 = 0
  R_B1E = 1, R_B3E = 2, R_CBE = 3, R_B1L = 4, R_B3L = 5, R_CBL = 6
  R_X1E = 7, R_X3E = 8, R_CXE = 9, R_X1L = 10, R_X3L = 11, R_CXL = 12
  R_Y1E = 13, R_Y3E = 14, R_CYE = 15
  NREAD = 16

  ' CT upper-long epochs the arms read in
  HI_BOOT = 0, HI_BAND = LAG, HI_CLOSE = LAG + 1, HI_AFTER = LAG + 2

  ' predictions, fixed before the run
  P_BAND   = LAG                  ' in the band: behind by every missed wrap (FALSE: 0)
  P_CLOSED = 0                    ' after the closing wrap: current (FALSE: LAG-1 or LAG)
  P_CTRL   = 0                    ' cog 5 (group 1): always 0, else RIG FAIL

VAR ' ---- Test State ----
  long mailboxControl[MB_LONGS]   ' cog 5's mailbox
  long mailboxCogA[MB_LONGS]      ' cog 1's mailbox
  long mailboxCogB[MB_LONGS]      ' cog 3's mailbox
  long requestSeq                 ' request counter, never 0 once used
  long wrapsSeen                  ' lower-long wraps cog 4 watched since it started (C2)
  long prevCtLo                   ' last CT lower long cog 4 saw (C2)
  long bRigBad                    ' TRUE once any judged control has failed
  long readStatus[NREAD]          ' per slot: ST_* status
  long readD[NREAD]               ' per slot: agreed D
  long readBracketFails[NREAD]    ' per slot: LO-BRACKET failure count
  long bHalted                    ' TRUE once a RIG FAIL has halted the run: later steps are skipped
  long ctrlStack[CTRL_STACK_LONGS]  ' the controller's Spin2 stack

PUB main() | ctHi, ctLo, cogMask
'' Cog 0: check the boot state, start the controller in cog 4, then stop
'' this cog, so no cog of 0-3 runs.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local ctHi - cog 0's own CT upper long, from ct64()
' @local ctLo - cog 0's own CT lower long, from ct64()
' @local cogMask - running-cog bitmask, from runmask()

  ' ---- C4: boot state -------------------------------------------------
  ctHi, ctLo := ct64()
  cogMask := runmask()
  debug("=== Erratum E3 GROUP-0 IDLE BAND TEST: cogs 0-3 empty through ", udec_(LAG), " wraps, then cogs 1 and 3 started ===")
  debug("boot (cog 0): CT=", uhex_long_(ctHi), "_", uhex_long_(ctLo), " running cogs=", ubin_byte_(cogMask))
  if ctHi <> HI_BOOT
    debug("RIG FAIL: CT hi at boot expected 0, got ", uhex_long_(ctHi), " - no fresh reset; reload with reset")
    debug("HALTED - no verdict")
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
    repeat
  elseif cogMask <> M_BOOT
    debug("RIG FAIL: running cogs at boot expected ", ubin_byte_(M_BOOT), ", got ", ubin_byte_(cogMask))
    debug("HALTED - no verdict")
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
    repeat

  debug("cog 0: starting the controller in cog 4, then stopping cog 0")
  cogspin(CTRL_COG, controller(), @ctrlStack)
  cogstop(BOOT_COG)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI controller() | ctHi, ctLo
' Cog 4: the whole test from here on, with cog 4 as the reference.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local ctHi - cog 4's own CT upper long, from ct64()
' @local ctLo - cog 4's own CT lower long, from ct64()

  ' A RIG FAIL halts the run (bHalted): a guard follows every step that
  ' can halt (wait_until, expect_mask), so every path ends at finish().
  ctHi, ctLo := ct64()
  prevCtLo := ctLo
  wrapsSeen := 0
  debug("controller (cog 4) up: CT=", uhex_long_(ctHi), "_", uhex_long_(ctLo))
  debug("predictions: band D=", udec_(P_BAND), " (FALSE 0); after the closing wrap D=0 (FALSE ", udec_(LAG - 1), " or ", udec_(LAG), "); cog5 D=0 always")
  if ctHi <> HI_BOOT
    debug("RIG FAIL: CT hi at controller start expected 0, got ", uhex_long_(ctHi))
    halt()

  ' ---- control sampler: cog 5 (group 1); cogs 0-3 must be empty -------
  if bHalted == FALSE
    start_sampler(REF_SMP_COG, @mailboxControl)
    waitms(COG_SETTLE_MS)
    expect_mask(M_REF)

  if bHalted == FALSE
    wait_until(HI_BOOT, LOWIN, M_REF)
  if bHalted == FALSE
    reading(R_C0, string("R0  cog5 hi=0"), @mailboxControl)

  ' ---- group 0 empty across LAG wraps ---------------------------------
  if bHalted == FALSE
    debug("--- waiting for CT hi=", udec_(HI_BAND), " with cogs 0-3 all stopped (~", udec_(LAG * 2147 / 100), " s) ---")
    wait_until(HI_BAND, LOWIN, M_REF)

  ' ---- the band opens: cogs 1 and 3 started ---------------------------
  if bHalted == FALSE
    start_sampler(SMP_COG_A, @mailboxCogA)
    start_sampler(SMP_COG_B, @mailboxCogB)
    waitms(COG_SETTLE_MS)
    expect_mask(M_BAND)
  if bHalted == FALSE
    debug("--- cogs 1 and 3 started (first group-0 cogs since cog 0 stopped): band open ---")
    reading(R_B1E, string("B1E cog1 band early"), @mailboxCogA)
    reading(R_B3E, string("B3E cog3 band early"), @mailboxCogB)
    reading(R_CBE, string("CBE cog5 band early"), @mailboxControl)

  if bHalted == FALSE
    wait_until(HI_BAND, LATE, M_BAND)
  if bHalted == FALSE
    reading(R_B1L, string("B1L cog1 band late"), @mailboxCogA)
    reading(R_B3L, string("B3L cog3 band late"), @mailboxCogB)
    reading(R_CBL, string("CBL cog5 band late"), @mailboxControl)

  ' ---- the closing wrap: cogs 1 and 3 run through it ------------------
  if bHalted == FALSE
    debug("--- waiting for CT hi=", udec_(HI_CLOSE), " with cogs 1 and 3 running (the closing wrap) ---")
    wait_until(HI_CLOSE, LOWIN, M_BAND)
  if bHalted == FALSE
    reading(R_X1E, string("X1E cog1 closed early"), @mailboxCogA)
    reading(R_X3E, string("X3E cog3 closed early"), @mailboxCogB)
    reading(R_CXE, string("CXE cog5 closed early"), @mailboxControl)

  if bHalted == FALSE
    wait_until(HI_CLOSE, LATE, M_BAND)
  if bHalted == FALSE
    reading(R_X1L, string("X1L cog1 closed late"), @mailboxCogA)
    reading(R_X3L, string("X3L cog3 closed late"), @mailboxCogB)
    reading(R_CXL, string("CXL cog5 closed late"), @mailboxControl)

  ' ---- one wrap later: still current ----------------------------------
  if bHalted == FALSE
    debug("--- waiting for CT hi=", udec_(HI_AFTER), " with cogs 1 and 3 running ---")
    wait_until(HI_AFTER, LOWIN, M_BAND)
  if bHalted == FALSE
    reading(R_Y1E, string("Y1E cog1 after early"), @mailboxCogA)
    reading(R_Y3E, string("Y3E cog3 after early"), @mailboxCogB)
    reading(R_CYE, string("CYE cog5 after early"), @mailboxControl)

  if bHalted == FALSE
    verdict()
  finish()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI verdict() | slotIdx, bBandOk, bClosedOk, bAnyInconclusive, bAnyBracket
' Print every reading slot's status, apply the control checks (C1/C5),
' then compare the group-0 readings with the predictions to produce the
' one-line VERDICT.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local slotIdx - reading-slot index while printing the summary table
' @local bBandOk - TRUE if all four band readings gave D = P_BAND
' @local bClosedOk - TRUE if all six readings after the closing wrap gave D = P_CLOSED
' @local bAnyInconclusive - TRUE if a group-0 reading had disagreeing or too few pairs
' @local bAnyBracket - TRUE if a group-0 reading failed LO-BRACKET

  debug("=== SUMMARY (D = cog4 hi - sampler hi; st 0=ok 1=lo-bracket-fail 2=mixed 3=short 4=timeout) ===")
  repeat slotIdx from 0 to NREAD - 1
    debug("slot ", udec_(slotIdx), ": D=", sdec_(readD[slotIdx]), " st=", udec_(readStatus[slotIdx]), " lo-bracket-fails=", udec_(readBracketFails[slotIdx]))

  ' ---- C1: every cog-5 control reading must be ok with D = 0 ----------
  ctrl(R_C0, string("R0"))
  ctrl(R_CBE, string("CBE"))
  ctrl(R_CBL, string("CBL"))
  ctrl(R_CXE, string("CXE"))
  ctrl(R_CXL, string("CXL"))
  ctrl(R_CYE, string("CYE"))
  ' ---- C5: the group-0 samplers must have answered --------------------
  if group0_status_any(ST_TIMEOUT) == TRUE
    debug("RIG FAIL: a group-0 sampler (cog 1 or cog 3) did not answer")
    bRigBad := TRUE

  bAnyInconclusive := group0_status_any(ST_MIXED) or group0_status_any(ST_SHORT)
  bAnyBracket := group0_status_any(ST_BRACKET)
  bBandOk := readD[R_B1E] == P_BAND and readD[R_B3E] == P_BAND and readD[R_B1L] == P_BAND and readD[R_B3L] == P_BAND
  bClosedOk := readD[R_X1E] == P_CLOSED and readD[R_X3E] == P_CLOSED and readD[R_X1L] == P_CLOSED and readD[R_X3L] == P_CLOSED and readD[R_Y1E] == P_CLOSED and readD[R_Y3E] == P_CLOSED

  if bRigBad == TRUE
    debug("NO VERDICT: rig failed (see RIG FAIL lines)")
  elseif bAnyInconclusive == TRUE
    debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - a group-0 reading had disagreeing pairs or too few valid pairs (st>=2 above)")
  elseif bAnyBracket == TRUE
    debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - a group-0 plain GETCT fell outside cog 4's bracket: group-0 LOWER copy not current (predicted current)")
  elseif bBandOk == TRUE and bClosedOk == TRUE
    debug("VERDICT: CONFIRMED - cogs 1 and 3 D=", udec_(P_BAND), " in the band, D=0 after the ONE closing wrap and the wrap after: cogs 0-3 show the same band")
  elseif bBandOk == FALSE
    debug("VERDICT: REFUTED (band) - band D: B1E=", sdec_(readD[R_B1E]), " B3E=", sdec_(readD[R_B3E]), " B1L=", sdec_(readD[R_B1L]), " B3L=", sdec_(readD[R_B3L]), " (pred ", udec_(P_BAND), ")")
  else
    debug("VERDICT: REFUTED (closing) - after the closing wrap D: X1E=", sdec_(readD[R_X1E]), " X3E=", sdec_(readD[R_X3E]), " X1L=", sdec_(readD[R_X1L]), " X3L=", sdec_(readD[R_X3L]), " Y1E=", sdec_(readD[R_Y1E]), " Y3E=", sdec_(readD[R_Y3E]), " (pred 0)")

PRI group0_status_any(stCode) : bFound
' True when any group-0 (cog 1 or cog 3) reading slot has status stCode.
'
' @param stCode - an ST_* status code
' @returns bFound - TRUE if at least one group-0 slot has that status

  bFound := FALSE
  if readStatus[R_B1E] == stCode or readStatus[R_B3E] == stCode or readStatus[R_B1L] == stCode or readStatus[R_B3L] == stCode
    bFound := TRUE
  if readStatus[R_X1E] == stCode or readStatus[R_X3E] == stCode or readStatus[R_X1L] == stCode or readStatus[R_X3L] == stCode
    bFound := TRUE
  if readStatus[R_Y1E] == stCode or readStatus[R_Y3E] == stCode
    bFound := TRUE

PRI ctrl(slotIdx, pLabel)
' Check the cog-5 (group 1) control reading in slot slotIdx: st must be
' ST_OK and D must be P_CTRL (0), else RIG FAIL.
'
' @param slotIdx - reading-slot index (an R_* constant)
' @param pLabel - address of the reading's zero-terminated label, printed by zstr_()

  if readStatus[slotIdx] <> ST_OK or readD[slotIdx] <> P_CTRL
    debug("RIG FAIL: control cog 5 reading ", zstr_(pLabel), " expected D=0 st=0, got D=", sdec_(readD[slotIdx]), " st=", udec_(readStatus[slotIdx]))
    bRigBad := TRUE

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI reading(slotIdx, pLabel, pMailbox) | tries, validPairs, ackStatus, refHiBefore, refLoBefore, smpHi, smpLo, refHiAfter, refLoAfter, diffHi, bBracket, bMixed, baseD, bTimedOut
' One reading: NPAIRS valid request/answer pairs from one sampler.  Stores
' the agreed D, the status and the LO-BRACKET failure count into slot
' slotIdx.  Every pair is printed raw as it is taken.
'
' @param slotIdx - reading-slot index (an R_* constant)
' @param pLabel - address of the reading's zero-terminated label, printed by zstr_()
' @param pMailbox - sampler mailbox base address ([0]=req [1]=hi [2]=lo [3]=ack)

' Local Variables:
' @local tries - request attempts made so far, up to MAXTRY
' @local validPairs - valid (in-window) pairs taken so far, target NPAIRS
' @local ackStatus - take_pair() ack status for the current attempt (ACK_SEEN or ACK_NONE)
' @local refHiBefore - cog 4's own CT upper long, before the request (refB)
' @local refLoBefore - cog 4's own CT lower long, before the request (refB)
' @local smpHi - sampler's CT upper long for the current attempt
' @local smpLo - sampler's CT lower long for the current attempt
' @local refHiAfter - cog 4's own CT upper long, after the ack (refA)
' @local refLoAfter - cog 4's own CT lower long, after the ack (refA)
' @local diffHi - D for the current pair (refHiBefore - smpHi)
' @local bBracket - LO-BRACKET result for the current pair (refLoBefore < smpLo < refLoAfter)
' @local bMixed - TRUE once two valid pairs disagree on D
' @local baseD - D agreed across all valid pairs so far (from the first pair)
' @local bTimedOut - TRUE once take_pair() times out, to skip the post-loop scoring

  tries := validPairs := baseD := 0
  bMixed := FALSE
  bTimedOut := FALSE
  readBracketFails[slotIdx] := 0
  repeat while validPairs < NPAIRS and tries < MAXTRY
    tries++
    requestSeq++
    ackStatus, refHiBefore, refLoBefore, smpHi, smpLo, refHiAfter, refLoAfter := take_pair(pMailbox, requestSeq, clkfreq / ACK_TIMEOUTS_PER_SEC)
    if ackStatus == ACK_NONE
      debug(zstr_(pLabel), " TIMEOUT: sampler did not ack request ", udec_(requestSeq))
      readStatus[slotIdx] := ST_TIMEOUT
      readD[slotIdx] := 0
      bTimedOut := TRUE
      quit
    if refHiBefore <> refHiAfter or isInWindow(refLoBefore) == FALSE or isInWindow(smpLo) == FALSE or isInWindow(refLoAfter) == FALSE
      debug(zstr_(pLabel), " try ", udec_(tries), " DISCARD (outside window) ref=", uhex_long_(refHiBefore), "_", uhex_long_(refLoBefore), " smp=", uhex_long_(smpHi), "_", uhex_long_(smpLo), " ref2=", uhex_long_(refHiAfter), "_", uhex_long_(refLoAfter))
      next
    diffHi := refHiBefore - smpHi
    bBracket := (refLoBefore +< smpLo) and (smpLo +< refLoAfter)
    if bBracket == FALSE
      readBracketFails[slotIdx]++
    if validPairs == 0
      baseD := diffHi
    elseif diffHi <> baseD
      bMixed := TRUE
    validPairs++
    debug(zstr_(pLabel), " p", udec_(validPairs), " ref=", uhex_long_(refHiBefore), "_", uhex_long_(refLoBefore), " smp=", uhex_long_(smpHi), "_", uhex_long_(smpLo), " ref2=", uhex_long_(refHiAfter), "_", uhex_long_(refLoAfter), " D=", sdec_(diffHi), " lo-bracket=", udec_(bBracket & BOOL_BIT))
  if bTimedOut == FALSE
    readD[slotIdx] := baseD
    if validPairs < NPAIRS
      readStatus[slotIdx] := ST_SHORT
    elseif bMixed == TRUE
      readStatus[slotIdx] := ST_MIXED
    elseif readBracketFails[slotIdx] <> 0
      readStatus[slotIdx] := ST_BRACKET
    else
      readStatus[slotIdx] := ST_OK
    debug(zstr_(pLabel), " => D=", sdec_(baseD), " status=", udec_(readStatus[slotIdx]), " valid pairs=", udec_(validPairs), " tries=", udec_(tries))

PRI isInWindow(loVal) : bInWindow
' True when loVal falls inside the sample window [LOWIN, HIWIN] -- well
' clear of a 32-bit wrap.
'
' @param loVal - lower-long value to test
' @returns bInWindow - TRUE if loVal is in [LOWIN, HIWIN], FALSE otherwise

  bInWindow := (loVal +>= LOWIN) and (loVal +<= HIWIN)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI take_pair(pMailbox, reqSeq, tmo) : ackStatus, refHiBefore, refLoBefore, smpHi, smpLo, refHiAfter, refLoAfter | tmoStart, tmoNow, pAck, ackSeq, pHi, pLo
' One request/answer transaction with the sampler at pMailbox, entirely
' in the controller's PASM (cog-exec), waiting at most tmo clocks for the
' ack.  Causal order: refB -> req write -> (sampler GETCT WC, GETCT,
' writes, ack) -> ack seen -> sampler longs read -> refA.
'
' @param pMailbox - sampler mailbox base address ([0]=req [1]=hi [2]=lo [3]=ack)
' @param reqSeq - request sequence number to write, and to wait for as the ack
' @param tmo - timeout, in clocks, to wait for the ack
' @returns ackStatus - ACK_SEEN if the sampler acked within tmo, else ACK_NONE (rest of the returns 0)
' @returns refHiBefore - cog 4's own CT upper long, read before the request (refB)
' @returns refLoBefore - cog 4's own CT lower long, read before the request (refB)
' @returns smpHi - sampler's CT upper long
' @returns smpLo - sampler's CT lower long
' @returns refHiAfter - cog 4's own CT upper long, read after the ack (refA)
' @returns refLoAfter - cog 4's own CT lower long, read after the ack (refA)

' Local Variables:
' @local tmoStart - GETCT timestamp at request time, for the timeout wait
' @local tmoNow - GETCT timestamp on each poll, for the timeout wait
' @local pAck - hub address of the mailbox ack long
' @local ackSeq - request sequence number read back from the mailbox ack long
' @local pHi - hub address of the mailbox hi long
' @local pLo - hub address of the mailbox lo long

  ackStatus := ACK_NONE
  refHiBefore := 0
  refLoBefore := 0
  smpHi := 0
  smpLo := 0
  refHiAfter := 0
  refLoAfter := 0
  pHi := pMailbox + MB_HI_OFS
  pLo := pMailbox + MB_LO_OFS
  pAck := pMailbox + MB_ACK_OFS
  org
                getct   refHiBefore     wc      ' reference upper long, before
                getct   refLoBefore             ' reference lower long
                wrlong  reqSeq, pMailbox        ' request
                getct   tmoStart
.wait           rdlong  ackSeq, pAck
                cmp     ackSeq, reqSeq  wz
        if_z    jmp     #.got
                getct   tmoNow
                sub     tmoNow, tmoStart
                cmp     tmoNow, tmo     wc
        if_c    jmp     #.wait
                ret                             ' timeout: ackStatus stays ACK_NONE
.got            rdlong  smpHi, pHi
                rdlong  smpLo, pLo
                getct   refHiAfter      wc      ' reference upper long, after
                getct   refLoAfter
                mov     ackStatus, #ACK_SEEN
  end

PRI ct64() : ctHi, ctLo
' The calling cog's own 64-bit CT, read GETCT WC (upper long) then GETCT
' (lower long), the order the sampler uses.
'
' @returns ctHi - the calling cog's CT upper long
' @returns ctLo - the calling cog's CT lower long

  org
                getct   ctHi            wc
                getct   ctLo
  end

PRI ct_track() : ctHi, ctLo
' ct64() plus control C2: RIG FAIL if cog 4's upper long ever disagrees
' with the number of lower-long wraps cog 4 itself watched since it
' started.
'
' @returns ctHi - cog 4's own CT upper long
' @returns ctLo - cog 4's own CT lower long

  ctHi, ctLo := ct64()
  if ctLo +< prevCtLo
    wrapsSeen++
  prevCtLo := ctLo
  if isInWindow(ctLo) == TRUE and ctHi <> wrapsSeen
    debug("RIG FAIL: cog 4 CT hi=", uhex_long_(ctHi), " but cog 4 watched ", udec_(wrapsSeen), " lower-long wraps since it started - reference upper long not current")
    halt()

PRI wait_until(targetHi, minLo, expMask) | ctHi, ctLo, cogMask, ctTick, lastCtTick
' Poll cog 4's own CT until hi == targetHi and lo >= minLo, RIG FAIL (and
' halt) if the running-cog mask leaves expMask at any poll of the wait
' (C3) or on a hi overshoot; prints an "alive" line on every 2^28-clock
' tick while it waits. A halt (here or in ct_track()) quits the wait.
'
' @param targetHi - CT hi value to wait for
' @param minLo - minimum CT lo value to wait for, once hi == targetHi
' @param expMask - running-cog bitmask expected (bit N set = cog N running)

' Local Variables:
' @local ctHi - cog 4's own CT upper long, from ct_track()
' @local ctLo - cog 4's own CT lower long, from ct_track()
' @local cogMask - running-cog bitmask, from runmask()
' @local ctTick - ctHi and the top nibble of ctLo packed together, to throttle "alive" lines
' @local lastCtTick - ctTick at the last "alive" line, to detect a new tick

  lastCtTick := -1
  repeat
    ctHi, ctLo := ct_track()
    if bHalted == TRUE
      quit
    cogMask := runmask()
    if cogMask <> expMask
      debug("RIG FAIL: running cogs expected ", ubin_byte_(expMask), " got ", ubin_byte_(cogMask), " at CT ", uhex_long_(ctHi), "_", uhex_long_(ctLo))
      halt()
      quit
    if ctHi > targetHi
      debug("RIG FAIL: overshoot, CT hi=", udec_(ctHi), " waiting for ", udec_(targetHi))
      halt()
      quit
    ctTick := (ctHi << NIB_BITS) | (ctLo >> ALIVE_SHIFT)
    if ctTick <> lastCtTick
      lastCtTick := ctTick
      debug("  alive CT=", uhex_long_(ctHi), "_", uhex_long_(ctLo), " wraps-seen=", udec_(wrapsSeen), " running=", ubin_byte_(cogMask))
  until ctHi == targetHi and ctLo +>= minLo

PRI expect_mask(expMask) | cogMask
' RIG FAIL (and halt) if the running-cog mask does not equal expMask at
' this instant.
'
' @param expMask - running-cog bitmask expected (bit N set = cog N running)

' Local Variables:
' @local cogMask - running-cog bitmask, from runmask()

  cogMask := runmask()
  if cogMask <> expMask
    debug("RIG FAIL: running cogs expected ", ubin_byte_(expMask), " got ", ubin_byte_(cogMask))
    halt()

PRI runmask() : cogMask | cogIdx
' Build the running-cog bitmask from cogchk() across all cogs.
'
' @returns cogMask - bit N set if cog N is running

' Local Variables:
' @local cogIdx - cog number being tested

  cogMask := 0
  repeat cogIdx from 0 to COG_COUNT - 1
    if cogchk(cogIdx) == TRUE
      cogMask |= 1 << cogIdx

PRI halt()
' RIG FAIL exit: print the HALTED line and set bHalted, so every later step
' of the controller is skipped and the run ends at its one finish() (no
' verdict is printed).
'

  debug("HALTED - no verdict")
  bHalted := TRUE

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path of the controller ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the
' run when END_SESSION or DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output
' (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI start_sampler(smpCog, pMailbox)
' Start the sampler in cog smpCog by its explicit number (never the
' free-cog form), with pMailbox in its PTRA.
'
' @param smpCog - the cog to start (0..7)
' @param pMailbox - sampler mailbox base address ([0]=req [1]=hi [2]=lo [3]=ack)

  coginit(smpCog, @sampler, pMailbox)

DAT ' ---- Sampler Cog Code ----
' Sampler (cog-exec).  PTRA = mailbox.  On each NEW request number it
' reads GETCT WC then GETCT (upper long first), writes hi, lo, then ack.
                org     0
sampler         mov     s_last, #0
s_loop          rdlong  s_req, ptra
                cmp     s_req, s_last   wz
        if_z    jmp     #s_loop
                mov     s_last, s_req
                getct   s_hi            wc      ' this group's UPPER copy
                getct   s_lo                    ' this group's LOWER copy
                wrlong  s_hi, ptra[MB_HI_IDX]
                wrlong  s_lo, ptra[MB_LO_IDX]
                wrlong  s_req, ptra[MB_ACK_IDX] ' ack last: hi/lo already in hub
                jmp     #s_loop
s_last          long    0
s_req           res     1
s_hi            res     1
s_lo            res     1
